course: dictionary
lesson: 12285
title: Conventional: the usual way
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Conventional means usual and ordinary, done the way most people have done it for a long time. Its clues are often in the words around it, like «new», «electric» or «special», which show what it is being compared with. «My gran still uses a conventional oven, not a microwave.» The sentence sets the old, usual oven against the microwave, so conventional means the ordinary kind.
explain: A conventional person follows the normal ways and does not like to be different. «Grandma is conventional: she always wears a hat to church and never tries anything new.» Here conventional describes how she behaves: she likes safe, normal choices. Try your meaning in the sentence: usual and ordinary fits, so you know you are right.
explain: Conventional often matches with new or different things. «Electric cars are new, but most people still drive conventional cars.» Conventional cars are the usual kind that run on petrol, while electric cars are the new kind. When you see a word that sounds unfamiliar, look for the thing it is set against.
fact: Conventional means usual, ordinary and done the way most people have done it for a long time.
fact: A conventional person follows normal ways and rules and does not like to be different.
fact: Conventional ovens, cars and farming are the ordinary kinds, not the new or special ones.
fact: «Conventional wisdom» means the ideas most people accept as true.
fact: «Conventionally» is the adverb: «Most people conventionally eat breakfast in the morning» means in the usual way.
exercise: «My gran still uses a conventional oven, not a microwave.» What does conventional mean here? | A brand-new kind | *The usual, ordinary kind | A broken kind | A very small kind
exercise: «Electric cars are new, but most people still drive conventional cars.» What are conventional cars? | Cars that are very old and rusty | Cars that fly | Cars that only go very fast | *Cars with the usual kind of engine, not electric
exercise: «The shop sells ordinary bread, not special bread.» Find and copy one word that means conventional. | special | sells | bread | *ordinary
test: «The new method worked better than the conventional method.» What does conventional mean in this sentence? | Sleepy | *Usual and ordinary | Hidden | Wonderful
test: «Grandma is conventional: she always wears a hat to church and never tries anything new.» What does conventional suggest about Grandma? | She is always in a hurry | *She likes normal, usual ways and does not like change | She is very, very young | She is a famous inventor
exam: «The inventor ignored conventional methods and built a machine nobody had seen before.» What does conventional mean here? | Methods that are very old and broken | Methods that she invented herself | Methods that are secret | *The usual, ordinary methods most people use
